">Infused Edible<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"287\">SPICY CHEDDAR 10MG<\/td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"262\">Infused Edible<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"287\">BUTTER POPCORN 10MG<\/td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" width=\"262\">Infused Edible<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<\/tbody>\n<\/table>\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n<p><strong>There is no reason to believe that the dispensaries listed below had any knowledge that the creation and testing of these cannabis and cannabis products was unverifiable. <\/strong>It is believed the affected cannabis and cannabis products were sold between September 1, 2021, and March 1, 2022 by the following cannabis sales facilities:<\/p>\n<ol>\n<li>DIV Holdings DBA Jardin, 2900 E Desert Inn Rd Suite 102, Las Vegas, NV 89121 (License # 15398675340409721326)<\/li>\n<li>Essence Henderson LLC DBA Essence, 4300 E Sunset Rd Suite A2-A3, Henderson, NV 89014 (License # 19873661470522818141)<\/li>\n<li>Essence Tropicana LLC DBA Essence, 5765 W Tropicana Ave, Las Vegas, NV 89103 (License # 54135769938859220718)<\/li>\n<li>Euphoria Wellness LLC, 7780 S Jones Blvd Suite 105, Las Vegas, NV (License # 8913984716656554039635124)<\/li>\n<li>INYO Fine Cannabis Dispensary LLC, 2520 S Maryland Parkway Suite 2, Las Vegas, NV 89109 (License # 24344359150856320396)<\/li>\n<li>KYND-STRAINZ LLC DBA Mynt Cannabis Dispensary, 132 E 2nd St, Reno, NV 89501 (License # 46934338604709544132)<\/li>\n<li>Las Vegas Tribe of Paiute Indians DBA NuWu, 1235 Paiute Circle, Las Vegas, NV 89106 (59067229320122936181)<\/li>\n<li>Lemon Aide LLC, 340 Lemmon Dr Suite A, Reno, NV 89506 (License # 13244303247046007918)<\/li>\n<li>Livfree Wellness DBA The Dispensary, 50 N Gibson Rd Suite 170 &amp; 175, Henderson, NV 89014 (License # 08792343110299625005)<\/li>\n<li>Livfree Wellness DBA The Dispensary, 5347 S Decatur Blvd, Las Vegas, NV 89118 (License # 71224329369156133247)<\/li>\n<li>Livfree Wellness LLC DBA The Dispensary, 8605 S Eastern Ave, Las Vegas, NV 89123 (License # 64345737726226352455)<\/li>\n<li>Livfree Wellness LLC DBA The Dispensary, 100 W Plumb Ln, Reno, NV 89509 (License # 71702389611437559364)<\/li>\n<li>Nevada Holistic Medicine LLC DBA The Treehouse Vegas, 4660 S Decatur Blvd, Las Vegas, NV 89103 (License # 54535922714915823296)<\/li>\n<li>Reno-Sparks Indian Colony- Colony Enterprise Authority, 90 Auto Center Dr, Reno, NV 89511 (TR658198225338729107)<\/li>\n<li>Silver Sage Wellness LLC, 4626 W Charleston Blvd, Las Vegas, NV 89102 (License # 48309202150183437033)<\/li>\n<li>WSCC INC DBA Sierra Well, 3493 Arrowhead Dr, Carson City, NV 89706 (License # 37841996009528800127)<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<p>All cannabis and cannabis products properly sold by a licensed sales facility or dispensary should have a product label on the packaging.&nbsp; The name of the cultivation or production facility can be found on the label, typically near the top.<\/p>\n<p>The listed sales facilities are requested to display this bulletin in a conspicuous location on their premises for 30 days, to ensure their customers are aware of this information.<\/p>\n<p>There are no known reports of illness at this time. An investigation into the cannabis and cannabis products is ongoing and may result in additional public health and safety bulletins.<\/p>\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>The Nevada Cannabis Compliance Board (CCB) is hereby issuing Public Health and Safety Bulletin 2022-01on March 4, 2022 advising consumers and patients to avoid or take caution when consuming the cannabis and\/or cannabis products which are the subject of this notice.<\/p>\n","protected":false},"author":16,"featured_media":0,"comment_status":"closed","ping_status":"closed","sticky":false,"template":"","format":"standard","meta":{"_genesis_hide_title":false,"_genesis_hide_breadcrumbs":false,"_genesis_hide_singular_image":false,"_genesis_hide_footer_widgets":false,"_genesis_custom_body_class":"","_genesis_custom_post_class":"","_genesis_layout":"","footnotes":""},"categories":[10],"tags":[],"class_list":["post-3296","post","type-post","status-publish","format-standard","category-news","entry"],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/ccb.nv.gov\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts\/3296","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/ccb.nv.gov\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/ccb.nv.gov\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/post"}],"author":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/ccb.nv.gov\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/users\/16"}],"replies":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/ccb.nv.gov\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/comments?post=3296"}],"version-history":[{"count":0,"href":"https:\/\/ccb.nv.gov\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts\/3296\/revisions"}],"wp:attachment":[{"href":"https:\/\/ccb.nv.gov\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media?parent=3296"}],"wp:term":[{"taxonomy":"category","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/ccb.nv.gov\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/categories?post=3296"},{"taxonomy":"post_tag","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/ccb.nv.gov\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/tags?post=3296"}],"curies":[{"name":"wp","href":"https:\/\/api.w.org\/{rel}","templated":true}]}},{"id":3177,"date":"2021-11-05T22:05:00","date_gmt":"2021-11-05T22:05:00","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/ccbnvstaging.wpengine.com\/?p=3177"},"modified":"2021-11-05T22:06:44","modified_gmt":"2021-11-05T22:06:44","slug":"ccb-issues-summary-suspension-of-production-license","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"https:\/\/ccb.nv.gov\/ccb-issues-summary-suspension-of-production-license\/","title":{"rendered":"CCB Issues Summary Suspension of Production License"},"content":{"rendered":"\n\n\t<h2>CCB Issues Summary Suspension of Production License<\/h2>\n\n<p><strong>LAS VEGAS, NV &#8211; <\/strong>Pursuant to Nevada Cannabis Compliance Regulations (NCCR) 4.105, today the Nevada Cannabis Compliance Board (CCB) called an emergency telephonic board meeting to consider the summary suspension of the medical and adult-use production licenses held by Kindibles, LLC.<\/p>\n<p>Board members present voted unanimously to summarily suspend Kindibles, LLC (license # 45124567643462616034 and license # 19429852834178744891) effective immediately, citing a present threat to public health and safety.<\/p>\n<p>On 10\/20\/21, Board Agents visited the production facility of Kindibles, LLC, located in Clark County. After further investigation of production logs, Board Agents found thousands of additional products were added to a production run after testing, among other significant deficiencies. Per the NCCR, each addition of product should be considered a new production run, which requires a separate lab test. Additionally, Board Agents cited inaccurate inventory counts upon finding cannabis products physically present in the vault were not logged in the state&#8217;s seed-to-sale tracking system, Metrc.<\/p>\n<p>This resulted in <a href=\"https:\/\/ccb.nv.gov\/public-health-safety-bulletin-2021-2\/\">Public Health and Safety Bulletin 2021-2<\/a> issued by the CCB on November 5, 2021.<\/p>\n<p>Kindibles, LLC is required to submit a plan of correction to the CCB for approval within 10 business days in order to lift the order and shall not resume operations until the CCB has confirmed deficiencies identified in the order have been corrected.<\/p>\n<p>This is the third summary suspension issued by the CCB in 2021.<\/p>\n\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>Pursuant to Nevada Cannabis Compliance Regulations (NCCR) 4.105, the Nevada Cannabis Compliance Board (CCB) called an emergency telephonic board meeting to consider the summary suspension of the medical and adult-use production licenses held by Kindibles, LLC.<\/p>\n","protected":false},"author":16,"featured_media":0,"comment_status":"closed","ping_status":"closed","sticky":false,"template":"","format":"standard","meta":{"_genesis_hide_title":false,"_genesis_hide_breadcrumbs":false,"_genesis_hide_singular_image":false,"_genesis_hide_footer_widgets":false,"_genesis_custom_body_class":"","_genesis_custom_post_class":"","_genesis_layout":"","footnotes":""},"categories":[10],