rdance with the regulations.<\/p>\n<table>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"252\"><strong>Product <\/strong><\/td>\n<td width=\"126\"><strong>Production Run #<\/strong><\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"252\">KoKo Nuggz Chocolate Chip &#8211; 100mg &#8211; 10pk<\/td>\n<td width=\"126\">KN CC 21151<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"252\">KoKo Nuggz Kushberry- 100mg &#8211; 10pk<\/td>\n<td width=\"126\">KN KB 21151<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"252\">KoKo Nuggz Peanut Butter &#8211; 100mg &#8211; 10pk<\/td>\n<td width=\"126\">KN PB 21151<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"252\">KoKo Nuggz Red Velvet Cake- 100mg &#8211; 10pk<\/td>\n<td width=\"126\">KN RVC 21151<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"252\">KoKo Nuggz Kushberry- 100mg &#8211; 10pk<\/td>\n<td width=\"126\">KN KB 21266<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"252\">KoKo Nuggz Peanut Butter &#8211; 100mg &#8211; 10pk<\/td>\n<td width=\"126\">KN PB 21259<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"252\">KoKo Nuggz Birthday Cake- 100mg &#8211; 10pk<\/td>\n<td width=\"126\">KN BC 21243<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"252\">KoKo Nuggz Red Velvet Cake- 100mg &#8211; 10pk<\/td>\n<td width=\"126\">KN RVC 21243<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"252\">KoKo Nuggz Cookies &amp; Cream- 100mg &#8211; 10pk<\/td>\n<td width=\"126\">KN CKC 21243<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"252\">KoKo Nuggz Churro- 100mg &#8211; 10pk<\/td>\n<td width=\"126\">KN S-C 21288<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"252\">KoKo Nuggz Chocolate Chip &#8211; 100mg &#8211; 10pk<\/td>\n<td width=\"126\">KN CC 21243<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"252\">KoKo Nuggz Cookies &amp; Cream- 100mg &#8211; 10pk<\/td>\n<td width=\"126\">KN CKC 21147<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"252\">KoKo Nuggz OG Kush- 100mg &#8211; 10pk<\/td>\n<td width=\"126\">KN OGK 21259<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"252\">KoKo Nuggz OG Kush- 100mg &#8211; 10pk<\/td>\n<td width=\"126\">KN OGK 21147<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<\/tbody>\n<\/table>\n\n<p><strong>There is no reason to believe that the dispensaries listed below had any knowledge that the creation and testing of these edible products was unverifiable. <\/strong>It is believed the affected cannabis products were sold between June 1, 2021, and November 3, 2021 by the following Cannabis Sales Facilities:<\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Commerce Park Medical LLC dba Thrive Cannabis Marketplace, 3500 W. Sahara Blvd., Las Vegas, NV 89102 (license # 77505483208802721121)<\/li>\n<li>DIV Holdings LLC dba Jardin Premium Cannabis Dispensary, 2900 E Desert Inn Road #102, Las Vegas, NV 89121 (license # 15398675340409721326)<\/li>\n<li>GBS Nevada Partners LLC dba ShowGrow, 4850 South Fort Apache Road, Las Vegas, NV 89147 (license # 21647298952036123142)<\/li>\n<li>Integral Associates LLC dba Cookies on the Strip, 2307 S Las Vegas Blvd., Las Vegas, NV 89104 (license # 06347213896566425206)<\/li>\n<li>Las Vegas Tribe of Paiute Indians dba NuWu Cannabis Marketplace, 1235 Paiute Cir, Las Vegas, NV 89106<\/li>\n<li>MM Development Company Inc. dba Planet 13 Las Vegas, 2548 West Desert Inn Road #100, Las Vegas, NV 89109 (license # 62474301567586344896)<\/li>\n<li>Natural Medicine LLC dba Green Cannabis Co, 3650 S. Decatur Boulevard # 6 &amp; 7, Las Vegas, NV 89103 (license #48573289589249273073)<\/li>\n<li>Nevada Holistic Medicine LLC dba Vegas Treehouse, 4660 S. Decatur Boulevard, Las Vegas, NV 89103 (license #54535922714915823296)<\/li>\n<li>Silver State Relief LLC dba Silver State Relief, 175 E Greg St., Sparks, NV 89431 (license # 11443721033142554219)<\/li>\n<li>Silver State Relief LLC dba Silver State Relief, 1301 Financial Way, Fernley, NV 89408 (license #71064968398758187793)<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p>All cannabis and cannabis products properly sold by a licensed sales facility or dispensary should have a product label on the packaging.\u00a0 The production run number can be found on the label, typically near the top, directly below the facility information.<\/p>\n<p>The involved sales facilities are requested to display this bulletin in a conspicuous location on their premises for 30 days, to ensure their customers are aware of this information.<\/p>\n<p>There are no known reports of illness. An investigation into these products is ongoing and may result in additional public health and safety bulletins.<\/p>\n\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>The Nevada Cannabis Compliance Board (CCB) is hereby issuing Public Health and Safety Bulletin 2021-02 on November 5, 2021 advising consumers and patients to avoid or take caution when consuming the cannabis product which is the subject of this notice. <\/p>\n","protected":false},"author":16,"featured_media":0,"comment_status":"closed","ping_status":"closed","sticky":false,"template":"","format":"standard","meta":{"_genesis_hide_title":false,"_genesis_hide_breadcrumbs":false,"_genesis_hide_singular_image":false,"_genesis_hide_footer_widgets":false,"_genesis_custom_body_class":"","_genesis_custom_post_class":"","_genesis_layout":"","footnotes":""},"categories":[10],"tags":[],"class_list":["post-3176","post","type-post","status-publish","format-standard","category-news","entry"],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/ccb.nv.gov\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts\/3176","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/ccb.nv.gov\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/ccb.nv.gov\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/post"}],"author":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/ccb.nv.gov\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/users\/16"}],"replies":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/ccb.nv.gov\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/comments?post=3176"}],"version-history":[{"count":0,"href":"https:\/\/ccb.nv.gov\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts\/3176\/revisions"}],"wp:attachment":[{"href":"https:\/\/ccb.nv.gov\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media?parent=3176"}],"wp:term":[{"taxonomy":"category","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/ccb.nv.gov\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/categories?post=3176"},{"taxonomy":"post_tag","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/ccb.nv.gov\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/tags?post=3176"}],"curies":[{"name":"wp","href":"https:\/\/api.w.org\/{rel}","templated":true}]}},{"id":2955,"date":"2021-07-08T18:00:00","date_gmt":"2021-07-08T18:00:00","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/ccbnvstaging.wpengine.com\/?p=2955"},"modified":"2021-07-09T18:10:37","modified_gmt":"2021-07-09T18:10:37","slug":"public-health-and-safety-bulletin-2021-01","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"https:\/\/ccb.nv.gov\/public-health-and-safety-bulletin-2021-01\/","title":{"rendered":"Public Health and Safety Bulletin &#8211; 2021-01"},"content":{"rendered":"\n<h2>Public Health and Safety Bulletin 2021-1<\/h2>\n<p>The Nevada Cannabis Compliance Board (CCB) is hereby issuing Public Health and Safety Bulletin 2021-01 on July 8, 2021 advising consumers and patients to avoid or take caution when consuming the cannabis product which is the subject of this notice.<\/p>\n<p>The CCB has determined that the THC potency testing results reported by the independent cannabis testing laboratory MA Analytics (license # 81521595921502470043) may not accurately reflect the THC potency testing result for the following cannabis product:<\/p>\n<table>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"180\"><strong>Product <\/strong><\/td>\n<td width=\"132\"><strong>Production Run #<\/strong><\/td>\n<td width=\"348\"><strong>Production Facility<\/strong><\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"180\">Wyld &#8211; Raspberry Gummy<\/td>\n<td width=\"132\">RB B104<\/td>\n<td width=\"348\">Las Vegas Tribe of Paiute Indians (35786145068445853965)<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<\/tbody>\n<\/table>\n<p>There is no reason at this time to believe that the sales facilities or the production facility had any knowledge that the THC potency testing result may be inaccurate.<\/p>\n\n<p>It is believed the affected cannabis product was sold between June 25, 2021 and July 7, 2021 by the following Cannabis Sales Facilities:<\/p>\n<ol>\n<li>Nevada Holistic Medicine LLC dba Vegas Treehouse, 4660 S. Decatur Boulevard, Las Vegas, NV 89103 (license # 54535922714915823296)<\/li>\n<li>DE Dispensary Ops NV LLC dba Wallflower Cannabis House, 6540 Blue Diamond Road, Las Vegas, NV 89139 (license # 23003643426806888206)<\/li>\n<li>Acres Medical LLC dba Acres by Curaleaf, 2320 Western Ave, Las Vegas, NV 89102 (license # 11058209030610809158)<\/li>\n<li>Natural Medicine LLC dba Green Cannabis Co, 3650 S Decatur Blvd #7, Las Vegas, NV 89103 (license # 48573289589249273073)<\/li>\n<li>Euphoria Wellness LLC dba Euphoria Wellness, 7780 S Jones Blvd Suite 105, Las Vegas, NV 89139 (license # 84716656554039635124)<\/li>\n<li>Paradise Wellness Center LLC dba Las Vegas Releaf, 2244 Paradise Rd Las Vegas, NV 89104 (license # 54283805068313943868)<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<p>All cannabis and cannabis products properly sold by a licensed sales facility or dispensary should have a product label on the packaging.&nbsp; The production run number can be found on the label, typically near the top, directly below the facility information.<\/p>\n<p>The involved sales facilities should display this bulletin in a conspicuous location on their premises for 30 days, to ensure their customers are aware of this information.<\/p>\n<p>There are no known reports of illness. An investigation into the inaccurate results and reporting is ongoing and may result in additional public health and safety bulletins.<\/p>\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>The Nevada Cannabis Compliance Board (CCB) is hereby issuing Public Health and Safety Bulletin 2021-01 on July 8, 2021 advising consumers and patients to avoid or take caution when consuming the cannabis product which is the subject of this notice. <\/p>\n","protected":false},"author":16,"featured_media":0,"comment_status":"closed","ping_status":"closed","sticky":false,"template":"","format":"standard","meta":{"_genesis_hide_title":false,"_genesis_hide_breadcrumbs":false,"_genesis_hide_singular_image":false,"_genesis_hide_footer_widgets":false,"_genesis_custom_body_class":"","_genesis_custom_post_class":"","_genesis_layout":"","footnotes":""},"categories":[10],"tags":[],"class_list":["post-2955","post","type-post","status-publish","format-standard","category-news","entry"],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/ccb.nv.gov\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts\/2955","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/ccb.nv.gov\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/ccb.nv.gov\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/post"}],"author":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/ccb.nv.gov\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/users\/16"}],"replies":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/ccb.nv.gov\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/comments?post=2955"}],"version-history":[{"count":0,"href":"https:\/\/ccb.nv.gov\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts\/2955\/revisions"}],"wp:attachment":[{"href":"https:\/\/ccb.nv.gov\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media?parent=2955"}],"wp:term":[{"taxonomy":"category","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/ccb.nv.gov\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/categories?post=2955"},{"taxonomy":"post_tag","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/ccb.nv.gov\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/tags?post=2955"}],"curies":[{"name":"wp","href":"https:\/\/api.w.org\/{rel}","templated":true}]}},{"id":2649,"date":"2020-11-12T09:00:58","date_gmt":"2020-11-12T09:00:58","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/ccbnvstaging.wpengine.com\/?p=2649"},"modified":"2020-11-12T15:33:29","modified_gmt":"2020-11-12T15:33:29","slug":"ccb-among-founding-members-cannra","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"https:\/\/ccb.nv.gov\/ccb-among-founding-members-cannra\/","title":{"rendered":"CCB Among Founding Members of Cannabis Regulators Association"},"content":{"rendered":"\n<h2>CCB Among Founding Members of Cannabis Regulators Association<\/h2>\n<p>Today, state cannabis regulators from across the United States announced the formation of a non-partisan organization, the Cannabis Regulators Association (CANNRA), to better share institutional knowledge and regulatory best practices. Cannabis regulators from 19 states have joined in filing documents to establish CANNRA, which is being created in order to assist federal, state, and local jurisdictions that have approved or are weighing legalization of cannabis.<\/p>\n<p>\u201cThe Cannabis Regulators Association will provide a much needed forum for regulators to engage with each other to identify and develop best practices, create model policies that safeguard public health and safety, and promote regulatory certainty for industry participants,\u201d said Norman Birenbaum, CANNRA\u2019s inaugural president.<\/p>\n<p>For years, cannabis regulators across the country have relied on each other to share regulatory experiences, institutional expertise, and to provide assistance navigating the numerous evolving policy and regulatory issues associated with legalizing and regulating cannabis. Often the first step for state and local jurisdictions weighing legalization is to engage with regulators from established markets and programs. However, there has never been an organization to facilitate these interactions or help stakeholders find objective data and evidence-based approaches to policymaking and implementation.<\/p>\n<p>The Cannabis Regulators Association is not an advocacy group and takes no formal position for or against cannabis legalization, but rather seeks to provide government jurisdictions with unbiased information to help make informed decisions when considering whether or how to legalize or expand regulated cannabis.<\/p>\n<p>CANNRA will facilitate communication and information sharing between subject matter experts&nbsp;in regulatory approaches for industrial hemp, medical cannabis, and adult-use cannabis.&nbsp;This will include exchanges with research organizations, public health officials, policymakers, legal authorities, advocacy groups, and cannabis industry participants.<\/p>\n<p>\u201cThe association will strive to create and promote harmony and standardization across jurisdictions which choose to legalize and regulate cannabis,\u201d said Birenbaum. Birenbaum currently serves as the Director of Cannabis Programs for New York State.&nbsp; \u201cThe Cannabis Regulators Association will also work to ensure federal officials benefit from the vast experiences of states across the nation to ensure any changes to federal law adequately address states\u2019 needs and priorities,\u201d he said.<\/p>\n<p>CANNRA founding members include the principal cannabis regulators from 19 states: Colorado, Delaware, Hawaii, Illinois, Iowa, Louisiana, Maine, Maryland, Massachusetts, Michigan, Minnesota, <strong>Nevada<\/strong>, New Jersey, New York, North Dakota, Oregon, Rhode Island, Utah, and Washington.<\/p>\n<p><strong>&nbsp;<\/strong>\u201cThe CCB is proud to be a founding member of CANNRA, giving Nevada an active voice in critical state and federal conversations surrounding cannabis policy and regulation,\u201d <strong>said CCB Executive Director Tyler Klimas<\/strong>. \u201cWorking with state counterparts to advance important dialogue and serving as an executive officer provides a great opportunity to showcase Nevada\u2019s position as a leader in cannabis oversight.\u201d<\/p>\n<p>Additional state regulators are expected to soon join CANNRA; CANNRA anticipates providing membership opportunities for county and municipal cannabis regulators in the near future. Membership is limited to regulators and representatives from relevant government offices. Membership in CANNRA is not available to industry participants or advocacy organizations.<\/p>\n<p>CANNRA members will be able to access a national registry of member regulators, resources for cannabis policy development and staff training, and will have the ability to access, and participate in the development of model standards and best practices for cannabis regulation.<\/p>\n<p>Members will also be eligible to attend exclusive \u201cRegulator Roundtable\u201d conferences and programs, and receive legislative analyses, policy tracking data, and bulletins on current issues and events in the cannabis industry and regulatory arena.<\/p>\n<p>CANNRA\u2019s executive officers will include Norman Birenbaum, Director of Cannabis Programs for New York State as President; Rick Garza, Director of the Washington State Liquor and Cannabis Board as First Vice President; Jim Burack, Director of Colorado\u2019s Marijuana Enforcement Division as Second Vice President; Andrew Brisbo, Executive Director of Michigan\u2019s Marijuana Regulatory Agency as Third Vice President; and <strong>Tyler Klimas, Executive Director of Nevada\u2019s Cannabis Compliance Board<\/strong> as Secretary Treasurer.<\/p>\n<p>\u201cOur intent in forming this organization is to have CANNRA serve as a resource for policy makers, elected officials, researchers, and other stakeholders to engage with regulators from across the country and receive unbiased information and recommendations regarding the impact and implementation of cannabis policies,\u201d said Birenbaum.<\/p>\n<p>For more information about the Nevada Cannabis Compliance Board visit <a href=\"https:\/\/ccb.nv.gov\/\">ccb.nv.gov<\/a>.<\/p>\n<p>For more information about the Cannabis Regulators Association or to inquire about membership please visit <a href=\"http:\/\/www.Cann-RA.org\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">www.Cann-RA.org<\/a> or email <a href=\"mailto:info@Cann-RA.org\">info@Cann-RA.org<\/a>.<\/p>\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>The Nevada Cannabis Compliance Board (CCB) has taken significant steps to improve the agent card application process. <\/p>\n","protected":false},"author":16,"featured_media":0,"comment_status":"closed","ping_status":"closed","sticky":false,"template":"","format":"standard","meta":{"_genesis_hide_title":false,"_genesis_hide_breadcrumbs":false,"_genesis_hide_singular_image":false,"_genesis_hide_footer_widgets":false,"_genesis_custom_body_class":"","_genesis_custom_post_class":"","_genesis_layout":"","footnotes":""},"categories":[10],"tags":[],"class_list":["post-2649","post","type-post","status-publish","format-standard","category-news","entry"],"_links"